# Application Kconfig, sourced automatically by Zephyr for the app directory.
# Shared by every workspace under workspaces/* (each one's app/ is a symlink to
# this directory, embarch-dev-bench/design.md §2).
#
# **An app Kconfig replaces Zephyr's own root, it does not extend it**, so it
# has to `source "Kconfig.zephyr"` itself or every Zephyr symbol vanishes and
# the build aborts on the resulting warnings. Found the hard way adding the
# first symbol here.

mainmenu "embarch-dev-bench"

config EMBARCH_DEV_BENCH_PANIC_AT_HANDSHAKE
	bool "Deliberately k_panic() right after the handshake diagnostic"
	help
	  A debug-only build that crashes on purpose, to exercise decision 38's
	  fatal-error path — the one part of it that has never run (§4).
	  log_panic() switching to synchronous, lock-free writing is what should
	  carry a Zephyr crash dump to Core as LogLines, and nothing has
	  deliberately crashed this firmware since it was written.

	  The question it answers is specific: dev-bench resets mid-study while
	  transmitting a long StepResult, and no crash dump ever arrives. That is
	  either because the reset is not a Zephyr panic, or because this path
	  does not deliver. A build that panics on command distinguishes them —
	  a dump in dev-bench.log means the path works and the real reset is
	  something else (brownout and a watchdog lead the alternatives); no dump
	  means the path itself is broken and the absence of one during a real
	  reset says nothing.

	  Never enable this in a build meant to run a study: it panics at every
	  handshake, so no study can start.
	default n

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
